WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.493
The client goes on every managed
Windows device, deployed by Intune,

3
00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:09.862
and opens a tunnel to the service edge
after the user signs in to Entra.

4
00:00:09.862 --> 00:00:14.963
How many devices actually carry it is the
first metric every later step leans on.

5
00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:20.064
The Microsoft traffic profile is what makes
the real source address visible to Entra

6
00:00:20.064 --> 00:00:23.368
I D, and it is the prerequisite
for the compliant network

7
00:00:23.368 --> 00:00:27.176
check and universal tenant
restrictions, which come in Module 3.

8
00:00:27.176 --> 00:00:30.652
So in this module you package
the client the way Learn does,

9
00:00:30.652 --> 00:00:34.491
scope the profile to a pilot group,
turn on source I P restoration,

10
00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:38.900
and measure how much of the pilot's
traffic the service actually carries.
